Storage Library System V2.4 for OpenVMS

HIGHLIGHTS

o  OpenVMS AXP V1.5 support, including mixed VAX and AXP cluster
   environments

o  Additional support of DLT magazine loaders

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Storage Library System for OpenVMS VAX and AXP (SPD 29.67) software is
Digital's solution to managing the backup and archiving of critical
corporate data. System managers and users require safe backup of data, with
full and automated access to restore operations in the event of catastrophic
data loss. In addition, users need to be able to archive project files when
the projects are put on hold, or if data must be held for legal or
regulation purposes.

Storage Library System (SLS) is a layered software product designed to
manage collections of removable media and the devices associated with saving
and retrieving data stored on the media. In addition, the product provides
for the easy automation of backup tasks.

SLS V2.4 provides enhanced functionality with the addition of support for
OpenVMS AXP V1.5 and enhanced support of the Tx8x7 family of tape loader
devices.

V2.4 Features

This version introduces support for OpenVMS AXP V1.5, in AXP clusters, with
VAX machines in a mixed cluster environment or standalone. This enables
migration from pure VAX to mixed VAX and AXP environments, taking advantage
of AXP performance, yet preserving expertise gained with the Storage Library
System software on VAX systems.

V2.4 also provides for the continued support of Rdb database backups and
restores using the RMU/Backup utility, and expanded support of Tx8x7
magazine loader devices. These devices offer seven cartridge magazine
loaders for high capacity unattended backups. This software product
understands the concept of a cartridge magazine, and maintains an inventory
of the magazine so, upon restore requests, the correct cartridge will be
loaded. This capability significantly reduces the amount of time needed to
restore files. Magazine support plus the ability to perform fast positioning
to the Saveset containing the file to be restored makes Storage Library
System and the Tx8x7 products the best solution for unattended backup and
restores.

The Storage Library System can utilize Tx8x7 magazine loaders in either the
random slot or sequential slot selection mode.

For more product information, please consult the "TL820 5.2 Tbyte Digital
Linear Tape Library" article in the July 5, 1994, hardcopy issue of Customer
Update and the "Storage Library System (SLS) for OpenVMS V2.3" article in
the February 15, 1993, online issue of Customer Update.

BENEFITS

o  Lowers system management costs:
   - Through the "set and forget" backup policies, system managers are freed
     from the repetitive backup tasks.
   - Allows users to restore certain files, without system management
     intervention.

o  Increases data integrity and security:
   - Backups occur automatically per policy, assuring that proper copies of
     vital corporate data are maintained.
   - Keeps track of where files are saved automatically.

o  Supports a lights out computing environment
   - Automatically executes backups and archives to reflect company needs,
     then continues automatically.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

Storage Library System V2.4 for OpenVMS VAX software is available now and
will be on the September 1994 CD-ROM for OpenVMS VAX product. Storage
Library System V2.4 for OpenVMS AXP V1.5 is available now. The product is
a client/server product. Users are required to have at least one server
license. Client licenses are called SLS REMOTE. The Storage Library System
also supports the StorageTek ACS 4400 silo. The Storage Library System ACS
license is used for this purpose.

