Pegasus Program Announcement Expands ObjectBroker/COM Capabilities

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Program to add base class libraries, class inheritance, and cross
   language object sharing to the Digital/Microsoft Common Object Model
   (COM)

o  Allows binary interaction across different development environments and
   languages

o  Simplifies and enhances cross platform, multi-language software
   development tasks

PROGRAM DESCRIPTION

Pegasus is designed to provide advanced capabilities on top of the Digital/
Microsoft Common Object Model (COM). COM is an open architecture for cross
platform development of client/server applications based on object oriented
technology. Linking Microsoft's OLE technology on the desktop to Digital's
ObjectBroker software on servers and desktops alike, COM enables
shrink-wrapped desktop development tools (e.g., Microsoft Visual Basic and
Visual C++, PowerBuilder) and desktop applications (e.g., Microsoft Excel,
Lotus Ami Pro) supporting COM/OLE interfaces to be automatically network
enabled for transparent use with ObjectBroker software.

Features being added to COM as part of Pegasus include a base class library
that's programming language independent. This provides common functions
defined as objects that can be invoked by the developer, eliminating the
need to create these objects. Examples of the objects to be provided include
streams, files, and name spaces.

Other capabilities being added to COM are class structures and class
inheritance. In traditional tightly integrated development environments,
developers reuse previously developed code and add their own extensions
through a process called inheritance.

Pegasus enhances COM by adding the ability to use classes and multiple
inheritance when creating COM software components. Developers can specialize
existing COM components using inheritance, even if they do not have the
component's source code. Users can now choose their development style based
on what they need, not based on limitations of their tools.

Another capability being announced as part of Pegasus is cross language
object sharing.

Elements of Pegasus will become available in six to nine months as part of a
strategic advanced developer's kit.

BENEFITS

COM is the object model that will be deployed in all future Microsoft
operating systems, providing the technology needed to make OLE and other
functions possible. As such, it is of vital interest to software developers
focused on the desktop, as well as to the end user community with millions
of desktops installed. COM has many features that are ideally suited to
desktop environments, including speed, interoperability across different
development environments, and graceful management of version differences
across a loosely coupled desktop environment.

The real benefit of COM, which Pegasus enhances, is a common object oriented
environment that is applicable across the enterprise -- from sharing
documents on Windows desktops to large UNIX software development projects. A
consistent, pervasive OO model greatly simplifies application software to
improve application scalability and integration, and facilitates the
creation and usage of standard, binary-replacable COM software components.

