PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The RoamAbout Access Point (SPD 51.38.01) and RoamAbout PCMCIA Wireless
Network Adapter (SPD 45.71.03) software products are now available with new
features. These include:

o  Roaming -- Portable PC users can move from the coverage area of one
   RoamAbout Access Point to the coverage area of another. The Access Points
   provide graceful handoff between coverage cells so that users do not lose
   their network connection.

o  Network Operating System Support -- The DOS ODI and NDIS V2.0.1 drivers
   included with the Network Adapter support the common network operating
   systems such as NetWare, PATHWORKS, and LAN Manager software.

o  SNMP Management -- A set of SNMP Management Information Bases allows
   users on any SNMP Network Management Station to manage the Access Point.

o  DEChub Support -- The Access Point can be used in the DEChub 90 and
   DEChub 900 environments, with configuration and management through the
   DEChub utilities.

The RoamAbout PCMCIA Wireless Network Adapter allows mobile PC users to
communicate with each other and access the wired LAN through the RoamAbout
Access Point.

For a full description of these products, please consult the product
announcement in the February 14, 1994, issue of Customer Update.

BENEFITS

The RoamAbout products support dynamic work environments, temporary offices,
difficult wiring environments, and untethered roaming users.

