VT520 Monochrome and VT525 Color Multisession Text Terminals

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Program compatible with the VT510, VT420, VT420 PCTerm, VT320, VT220,
   VT100, and VT52

o  Supports both Digital and WYSE type connectors and communications
   protocols

o  Works with more than 30 operating systems

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The VT520 monochrome and the VT525 color terminals are high quality, high
reliability, multisession text terminals. They have plug and play emulations
and have been tested with more than 30 operating systems. They were built to
meet international requirements and standards and to support 25 languages.
The VT520 and the VT525 can operate in any environment throughout a
worldwide organization. They also include complete keyboard programmability
and accessability aids.

Other features include:

o  Sculptured and tactile keyboard -- ergonomics appreciated by users.
o  "Sticky keys" input method for physically challenged users.
o  Zero font preference -- user selectable for easier recognition of
   characters.
o  High resolution and 73 Hz refresh rate, 802 x 432 resolution --
   flicker-free, clear display.
o  Overscan -- takes away the black border in reverse video.
o  VT525 -- full color text capacity, 16 colors; user selectable, easier
   character recognition.
o  VT525 -- choice of 14-inch, 15-inch, or 17-inch color SVGA monitor.
o  VT525 ANSI color text capatibility -- no modifications necessary to most
   applications.
o  VT525 -- ASCII color emulation.
o  VT525 -- color support for monochrome applications.
o  Advanced functionality -- every key on the keyboard is programmable up to
   eight levels. The VT500 family also features down-loadable macros; status
   and indicator lines; off-screen memory; horizontal and vertical
   scrolling; rectangular area operations; programmable banner; local
   copy/paste; built-in clock and calculator; and snap-in cartridge for easy
   firmware upgrades -- tools to improve productivity, off-load the host,
   and increase ease of use.

BENEFITS

o  Plug and play compatible with virtually all text applications and host
   systems. Users can replace their existing terminals with VT500 series
   terminals without making changes to their applications, operating
   systems, connectors, wiring, communication devices, or software.

o  Independent multisessions, dynamic page allocation, split screen viewing,
   icon session status indicators, and 8 pages of memory expandable to 20.

o  Standards compliant Energy Star and TCO, plus MPRII low emissions.

o  Easy programming, faster response time, reduction in communication
   traffic, and efficient screen management.

o  International scope -- meets all applicable regulatory standards
   worldwide, including MPRII (Low Emissions models). Five setup languages
   (English, French, German, Italian, and Spanish) and 25 languages
   supported.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The VT520 monochrome and VT525 color multisession text terminals are
available now. The VT520 is available in two basic models: International and
International Low Emissions. Low Emissions is built into the standard VT525
model. Northern and southern hemisphere versions are available.

The VT520 International and International Low Emissions models are available
with white, green, or amber phosphor. Every model of the VT500 family has
complete programming functionality and supports all 70 keyboards and 25
language character sets.

When ordering a VT520, users need to select a monitor model and keyboard as
separate line items. When ordering a VT525, users need to order a monitor,
system box, and keyboard as separate line items. Power cords are included;
communication cables must be ordered separately. Multilingual (English,
German, Spanish, French, Italian, and Dutch) installation and operating
manuals are included with each terminal. A Programmer's Reference Manual is
available separately for applications programmers (EK-VT520-RM).

Substantial discounts are available when purchased in bulk (45 units) or by
full trailer loads (900 units).

