New and Updated Service Offerings

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Eight new services plus updates on two existing services

o  More flexible and consistent service offerings

SERVICES DESCRIPTION

The following new services are available:

o  Information Services -- Initially on CD-ROM, this service provides
   problem and solution information for use by system managers. The service
   primarily covers OpenVMS VAX and OpenVMS AXP systems in the initial
   CD-ROM.

o  User Application Support (replaces End User Support) -- Digital's User
   Application Support provides a single point of contact for technical
   information and usage assistance for today's most popular desktop
   applications written for the DOS/Windows environment, in addition to
   applications based on OpenVMS AXP and DEC OSF/1 AXP environments.

o  Developer Support (initial implementation in the U.S., Holland, and
   Germany) -- This service offers expert technical support for a range of
   software development environments. Users may access via telephone or
   electronically (direct dialing, Internet, or CompuServe) a highly skilled
   Developer Support Team. Another option for users is to subscribe to the
   Electronic Developer's Forum to exchange information with other users,
   and as it becomes available, search through an extensive developer
   knowledge database. Regular newsletters provide additional sources of
   information.

o  Interoperability Testing -- This service provides for testing of user
   requested multivendor configurations (such as hardware, operating
   systems, or applications) to ensure that they are functioning properly.

o  Software Update Distribution (previously known as Media Documentation and
   Distribution Service and Documentation Update Service) -- A subscription
   service that provides new versions of software binaries and documentation
   to users holding valid licenses. The service is available for individual
   products. Software Engineering Change Orders (ECOs) are made available
   for the following operating systems and layered product platform pairs:
   OpenVMS VAX, OpenVMS AXP, VAX ULTRIX, and DEC OSF/1 AXP platforms. For
   more information, consult the "Consolidated Software Engineering Change
   Order Distribution" article in this issue.

o  Product Disposition -- This service provides for the environmentally
   responsible disposition of computers and related electronic products,
   regardless of their manufacturer. Digital provides the user with a
   Product Disposition certificate upon receipt and validation of the
   product. This service is already available in some areas.

o  Services Engineering -- These services ensure that products developed by
   a user have serviceability attributes such as availability,
   interoperability, fault tolerance, repairability, and serviceability
   readiness.

o  LAN Management Support -- This service is designed to help users perform
   any routine system administrative tasks required for the day-to-day
   operation of a multivendor LAN environment. These tasks can include
   continuous monitoring and performing administrative tasks associated with
   the LAN. In addition, several supplementary features are offered as
   one-time services to resolve security, capacity, operational, or
   performance related problems. All LAN management services can be
   delivered onsite or remotely.

o  Revised Services -- In addition to the above new services, four services
   have been revised: Software Publishing, System Healthcheck, Availability
   Review, and Availability Partnership.

