o  Direct access from OpenVMS clients and servers, PATHWORKS clients, and
   LAT servers

o  No layered software required on Digital or IBM hosts

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

Forest Computer, based in Okemos, Michigan, has released the details of the
first product to be marketed under its agreement with Digital. (See the
August 1994 issue of Customer Update.) The Forest 5788 Network Resource uses
Digital Alpha AXP technology to deliver IBM interconnect services to
OpenVMS, PATHWORKS, DECnet, and LAT environments. The Forest 5788 is a
dedicated, turnkey gateway that is completely self-contained -- no
additional layered software is required on any of the interconnected hosts.

IBM interconnect services offered by the Forest 5788 include:

o  Digital VT terminal access to IBM mainframe and IBM AS/400 applications
   via DECnet and Digital's Local Area Transport (LAT) protocols.

o  IBM 3270 and IBM 5250 workstation access to OpenVMS and VMS applications
   via standard IBM protocols.

o  Attended or unattended file transfer.

o  Automatic queue-to-queue printer sharing.

o  Remote job submission to Digital and IBM systems.

o  Program-to-program communications in realtime.

o  Support for Digital PATHWORKS workstations.

o  Support for IBM PC and CA/400 workstations.

On the Digital side of the network, the Forest 5788 supports DECnet Phase IV
protocols, DECnet/OSI protocols, and LAT servers. No additional layered
software is required in any of the OpenVMS or PATHWORKS systems. The Forest
5788 is accessed using standard DEC network services such as the File Access
Listener (FAL), the SET HOST command, as well as other core DECnet and LAT
utilities.

On the IBM side of the network, IBM mainframe interaction is performed using
standard System Network Architecture (SNA) and Network Job Entry (NJE)
services. IBM AS/400 traffic is accommodated using native Advanced
Peer-to-Peer Networking (APPN) and Advanced Program-to-Program Communication
(APPC) connections. As with Digital systems, no additional layered products
are required on the IBM mainframes or IBM AS/400 systems. All standard IBM
operating systems are supported, and a single Forest 5788 can support both
IBM mainframe and IBM AS/400 traffic.

BENEFITS

o  Compatibility with DECnet and LAT networks.

o  Direct access from application systems, servers, workstations, PCs, and
   terminals servers.

o  Operating system independence.

o  No layered software required on any of the user's clients, servers, or
   application systems.

o  All communications overhead off-loaded from clients, servers, and
   application systems.

o  High performance, ease of use, reliability, and cost effectiveness.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The Alpha AXP based version of the Forest 5788 will be available worldwide
in October 1994. Contact Forest Computer for configuration assistance and a
product quote.

