Figure 1 shows the functional block diagram of Digital's AXPvme
64 single module computer. In most applications, computers of
this class are used to handle the real-time control of a complex
system. The computer uses the DECchip 21068, capable of 40
SPECfp92, as the base processor. It provides standard I/O: small
computer systems interface (SCSI-2), Ethernet, two serial ports,
and a VME 64 backplane bus interface as well as three
configurable timers. Further configuration of the module has been
made possible through provisions for two mezzanine modules. The
first contains dynamic random-access memory (DRAM) for program
and data storage. The second interfaces to the PCI bus and
provides the user the option of adding a custom interface to the
module.

