PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

POLYCENTER Manager on NetView V3.1 for DEC OSF/1 (SPD 53.57) provides a
comprehensive network management solution for heterogeneous multivendor
devices and open networks requiring Simple Network Management Protocol
(SNMP). It includes user oriented SNMP applications for fault,
configuration, and performance management; and standard application
programming interfaces (APIs) that allow software developers to seamlessly
integrate their multiprotocol applications. POLYCENTER Manager on NetView
software incorporates the guidelines and definitions programmers need to
create SNMP or CMIP applications that can work together to provide end to
end management of enterprise information systems.

V3.1 Enhancements

o  Extended data base support allowing users to choose and integrate a range
   of databases such as ORACLE, SYBASE, INFORMIX, DB/2, and Rdb in addition
   to current INGRES support.

o  Emergency backup for guaranteed operator coverage.

o  Ease of use improvements, including:
   - Improved node placement within map.
   - Multiple dynamic workspaces.
   - Expanded discovery and number of interfaces/node

o  Significant performance improvements.

o  New systems performance monitoring tool.

o  Incorporation of HP OpenView V3.3 enhancements and improvements.

BENEFITS

Digital's SNMP network users will have more flexibility and more powerful
network management capabilities when using the latest version of POLYCENTER
Manager on NetView V3.1 for DEC OSF/1 AXP. A considerable number of product
enhancements have been developed and implemented jointly by Digital and IBM
to improve management of heterogeneous multivendor network devices, while
increasing overall network management reliability.

Emergency backup for guaranteed operator coverage is now available and
allows users to define a backup for emergency failover to another network
manager which then assumes responsibility for continued management of the
network. The improvement in reliability will keep the network manageable and
help prevent costly network downtime for critical applications.

Users will benefit from significant improvements in operational performance
of non-IP and IP discovery, display, and management. Expanded discovery is
now capable of displaying up to 2000 interfaces per node, thus improving
network visibility of IP devices. Improvements to the end user interface
make the task of network management easier and includes multiple dynamic
workspaces, new event card layout, menu bar changes, dialog box
improvements, enhanced discovery, and improved node placement within the
network submap. A new systems performance monitoring tool is available that
provides monitoring of the NetView workstation resources and automated
commands to correct problems that may affect performance.

POLYCENTER Complimentary Solutions

The POLYCENTER NetView network management packages are preconfigured,
factory installed hardware and software systems built around the POLYCENTER
Manager on NetView for DEC OSF/1 software, orderable with a single part
number and shipped ready to run.

