Jabberwocky Toolkit V2.0

HIGHLIGHTS

o  Now available for DEC OSF/1, OpenVMS, and Windows platforms

o  New event driven tools enhance legacy application integration

o  StarStream products provide an incremental migration path from legacy
   applications to a three tier client/server architecture

PRODUCT DESCRIPTION

The Jabberwocky Toolkit V2.0 (SPD 54.42) focuses on application integration
at a user interface and business process redesign level. It provides rapid
solution development capability for an information technology environment
where many of the applications used do not conform to any accepted standards
based architecture. The Jabberwocky Toolkit uses rapid application
development (RAD) services, via an integrated set of user interface,
scripting, and terminal management tools for linking, integrating, and
representing business applications.

Dialogue Bus Runtime Services is for users who require support for Motif
based workstations. Dialogue Bus Application Server is for users who intend
to serve applications to a distributed PC environment. Additional products
can then be layered on these base packages to configure the runtime
environment as required.

BENEFITS

The Jabberwocky Toolkit allows users to make small, rapid, evolutionary
changes that build on systems that already exist. Each change is of minimal
risk, takes a short time to produce, and generates some return on the
investment while building toward the future. Users are able to follow an
incremental migration path from their legacy systems to an object oriented
three tier client/server environment.

AVAILABILITY AND ORDERING

The Jabberwocky Toolkit V2.0 is available now.

The Jabberwocky Toolkit V2.0, with the exception of StarStream for Windows,
is supported on OpenVMS VAX V6.0 or later and on OpenVMS AXP V1.5 or later
on Alpha AXP processors, and on DEC OSF/1 V2.0 or later on Alpha AXP
processors.

StarStream for Windows is supported on Windows V3.1 or later on 80386,
80486, and 80586 processors.

